                <pb facs="0601" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11651.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-23T15:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Constitutionalist Chief has requested me verbally to ask if the President
                    will consider receiving from him a High Commissioner authorized to treat upon
                    the state of affairs and clothed with full power, or, if not convenient to
                    receive such a Commissioner personally, that each appoint such a High
                    Commissioner for the purpose named.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
